# Frontend Accessibility Guard

Apply when changing **UI components, styles, reader themes, or interaction behavior** in the client.

**Docs:** `docs/styleguide/ui-styleguide.md`, `docs/styleguide/frontend-patterns.md`. Reader/dark/sepia global behavior may touch `client/src/index.css`—keep contrast and hover/readability regressions in mind.

## Required Checks

- Text-size modes remain functional (`Small`, `Medium`, `Large`, `XL`).
- High-contrast mode remains legible across touched views.
- Mobile menu/modal behavior keeps overlay + outside-click + Escape handling consistent.
- Touch target sizing remains usable on mobile.
- **Reader:** verse blocks and modals stay usable in **sepia + dark** combinations; avoid coupling reader surfaces to generic `hover:bg-slate-*` patterns—prefer **reader-scoped semantic classes** and `index.css` tokens (`docs/styleguide/ui-styleguide.md`).

## Style Consistency

- Prefer Tailwind utilities for component styling.
- Use global CSS only for shared primitives/tokens.
- Domain UI lives under **`client/src/features/*`** (e.g. `features/reader/`) when adding substantial flows; keep pages thin orchestrators per `frontend-patterns.md`.
- Keep style updates aligned with docs in `docs/styleguide/`.

## Pre-Commit

- Ensure UI behavior/documentation are updated together when UX changes.
